-- title:
--   Supersingular widths give a cyclic combinatorial component group
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $\iota$ a finite index type, and let $e\colon\iota\to\mathbb N$ be a family of weights. Suppose given an injective map $j\colon\iota\to K$ such that for every $s$ one has $e(s)=\mathtt{jWidth}(j(s))$, where $\mathtt{jWidth}(a)=3$ if $a=0$, $=2$ if $a=1728$ (and $a\neq 0$), and $=1$ otherwise. Write $X=\mathtt{characterLattice}\ \iota$ for the kernel of the degree map $\mathbb Z^{\iota}\to\mathbb Z$, $D\mapsto\sum_{s}D_s$, let $\mathtt{gramMap}\ e\colon X\to\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb Z}(X,\mathbb Z)$ be the map induced by restricting the bilinear form `widthPairing e` on $\mathbb Z^{\iota}$ to $X$ in both arguments, and let $\Phi(e)=\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb Z}(X,\mathbb Z)/\operatorname{im}(\mathtt{gramMap}\ e)$ with quotient map $\mathtt{componentGroupProj}\ e$. Then for every $s_0\in\iota$ the subgroup of $\Phi(e)$ generated by the class of the functional $e(s_0)\cdot(\gamma\mapsto\gamma(s_0))$ on $X$, i.e. the set of its integer multiples, is all of $\Phi(e)$; in other words, this single class generates $\Phi(e)$.
--
--   This is the combinatorial input for the component group of the Jacobian of a modular curve with supersingular reduction: when $(\iota,e)$ is the set of nodes of the special fibre weighted by the thicknesses $3,2,1$ attached to the $j$-invariants $0$, $1728$ and the remaining ones, the class of the difference of the two components generates the whole group. It is used in the construction of prolongation tuples for place specialisations at level one, via [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_comp_depthCompLaw_and_surjective_levelOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_comp_depthCompLaw_and_surjective_levelOne).
